			"products_sourced": "Per Pam, the following 5 people should be included on distribution list for Issara communications / Issues Reports:\n\n1. Pamela Batty, Pamela.Batty@burberry.com (UK) [VP Corporate Responsibility; Issara's most senior contact on sustainability side]\n2. Fred Wong, Fred.Wong@burberry.com (HK) [Fred has a good working relationship with Florence at TAL Group, Hong Kong-based....]\n3. William Tong, William.Tong@burberry.com (HK)[reports to Fred and HK team is more operational/implementation and compliance/performance focused compared to UK team who are more policy/process oriented] \n4. Jocelyn Wilkinson, Jocelyn.Wilkinson@burberry.com (UK) [possibly Pam's #2, and more seniority than Charlotte and Samantha] \n5. Charlotte Pestana, Charlotte.Pestana@burberry.com (UK) [replaced Chevon, but more junior and new to Burberry]\n\nNot specifically mentioned:\nIsabelle Von Watzdorf, Isabelle.VonWatzdorf@burberry.com (UK) [VP of Sourcing, Pam's equivalent from sourcing; seems to get Issara and our mode and is in-the-loop; from sourcing so commercial and different dept. than Pam] \nKim Lim, Kim.Lim@burberry.com  [Kim has a very good working relationship with Roger at TAL Group; based in HK?]\nNina Morley, Christina.Morley@burberry.com [not sure]\nSamantha [UK-based and more junior than other UK contacts]\n\nNote:\nChevon was the previous focal point for Issara who know our work well and was a champion but left Burberry. \n\n__________________________________\n\n- Simon Westin is responsible for TG1, TG2 and MCL\n- Roger is the TAL Group \"big boss\" who we believe had agreed to discussions about workers not paying fees and repayment; Simon possibly not part of that discussion \n\n__________________________________\n\nBurberry BRAC? Steering Committee\n\nComprised of 5 members \n- Rosey Hurst (Impactt), rosey@impacttlimited.com\n- Rachel Wilshaw, Ethical Trade Manager, Private Sector team, Campaigns, Policy and Influencing Team, Oxfam GB, rwilshaw@oxfam.org.uk\n- CEO of a small belt business, focused on sustainable materials\n- Someone focusing on environment (not in discussion on this topic)\n- Someone else",
